~ start
=> hub

~ hub
Ressa Quickfingers: See something open, or are you just looking?
- "You always notice the weak flank first." [if not QuestRegistry.is_active(QuestRegistry.RESSA_QUEST) and not QuestRegistry.is_done(QuestRegistry.RESSA_QUEST) /]
	do QuestRegistry.offer(QuestRegistry.RESSA_QUEST)
	Ressa Quickfingers: Of course I do. An opening is useful right up until it is bait.
	Ressa Quickfingers: Think about which kind you want me taking. Then ask again.
	=> hub
- "How should you judge an opening?" [if QuestRegistry.is_active(QuestRegistry.RESSA_QUEST) and not GameState.get_flag("party_ressa_quickfingers_resolved") /]
	Ressa Quickfingers: That is my question for you. I can take the gap before it closes, or I can close it before someone else pays for it.
	Ressa Quickfingers: Which do you expect from me?
	- "Take the opening while it exists. Hesitation wastes the advantage." [#consequence=Ressa treats a weak flank as an opportunity unless ordered otherwise.]
		do QuestRegistry.resolve_companion_quest("ressa-quickfingers", QuestRegistry.RESSA_QUEST, 6.0, "Told Ressa to take the opening before it closes")
		Ressa Quickfingers: Clear enough. If you want it left alone, say so before I reach it.
		=> END
	- "Close it when the party would pay. An advantage is not worth exposing everyone else." [#consequence=Ressa weighs the party's exposure before taking a weak flank.]
		do QuestRegistry.resolve_companion_quest("ressa-quickfingers", QuestRegistry.RESSA_QUEST, 6.0, "Told Ressa to protect the party before taking an opening")
		Ressa Quickfingers: Slower, then. Not slow. I can work with that.
		=> END
- "Not now." [if not GameState.get_flag("party_ressa_quickfingers_resolved") /]
	=> END
- "We understand each other." [if GameState.get_flag("party_ressa_quickfingers_resolved") /]
	Ressa Quickfingers: We understand the rule. That is enough.
	=> END
